#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124131 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf44a846-8458-5e2f-bef3-72cf87a6035f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intercepts of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/id #uuid "58966f53-5f83-5c86-8ffe-38ad0dffd2b3" :question/math-academy-id "e-12555" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\dfrac{(x-3)^2}9 + \\dfrac{(y+4)^2}{16} - \\dfrac{(z-5)^2}{25} = 1$, find its intercepts with the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n((x - 3)^{2})/(9) + ((0 + 4)^{2})/(16) - ((0 - 5)^{2})/(25) &= 1 \\\\\n((x - 3)^{2})/(9) + 1 - 1 &= 1 \\\\\n((x - 3)^{2})/(9) &= 1 \\\\\n(x - 3)^{2} &= 9 \\\\\nx - 3 &= ± \\sqrt{9} \\\\\nx &= 3 ± 3 \\\\\nx &= 0, 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(0,0,0)$ and $(6,0,0)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124227 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b079a5ff-e73a-592f-b16c-8740682538f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Domain of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/id #uuid "e85cfe0b-4ff6-5cce-9384-aeb930843b49" :question/math-academy-id "e-5265" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $(x-1)^2 + y^2 - \\dfrac{z^2}{4} = -1$, find the domain of $z = z(x,y)$." :question/worked-solution "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 1)^{2} + y^{2} - \\frac{z^{2}}{4} &= -1 \\\\\n(x - 1)^{2} + y^{2} + 1 &= \\frac{z^{2}}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{z^{2}}{4} &= (x - 1)^{2} + y^{2} + 1 \\\\\nz^{2} &= 4((x - 1)^{2} + y^{2} + 1) \\\\\nz &= ± 2\\sqrt{(x - 1)^{2} + y^{2} + 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2$, we have\n\n$$\n(x-1)^2 + y^2 + 1 \\geq 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is $\\mathbb R^2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124282 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d28eda1a-a90b-57e9-969a-eb36552e413e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Traces of Hyperboloids"}] :question/id #uuid "1fbe37ed-9022-5c44-851c-0e66fe2fb79f" :question/math-academy-id "e-6078" :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of two sheets\n$-\\dfrac{(x-5)^2}{8} + \\dfrac{y^2}{50} + (z-3)^2 = -1$\nand the plane $z = 4$ onto the $xy$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $z = 4$, we substitute $z = 4$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n- ((x - 5)^{2})/(8) + \\frac{y^{2}}{50} + (z - 3)^{2} &= -1 \\\\\n&= - ((x - 5)^{2})/(8) + \\frac{y^{2}}{50} + 1 =-1 \\\\\n- ((x - 5)^{2})/(8) + \\frac{y^{2}}{50} &= -2 \\\\\n((x - 5)^{2})/(8) - \\frac{y^{2}}{50} &= 2 \\\\\n((x - 5)^{2})/(16) - \\frac{y^{2}}{100} &= 1 \\\\\n((x - 5)^{2})/(4^{2}) - \\frac{y^{2}}{10^{2}} &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $4$ and $10$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124743 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b079a5ff-e73a-592f-b16c-8740682538f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Domain of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e5f94d8-e377-52d6-8fdd-991054d50053" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y): x^{2} + y^{2} \\le 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121478} {:answer/id #uuid "cb910829-dd76-553e-bfa6-5a522e989edb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y): x^{2} + y^{2} > 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121479} {:answer/id #uuid "2acfd3c0-352a-50c7-b5bc-6d486c378ccf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121480} {:answer/id #uuid "5543d032-a1cd-58a6-89b8-c785f98226e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y): x^{2} + y^{2} \\ge 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121481} {:answer/id #uuid "66a9fec6-53eb-5991-9279-4e9adc9d22f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y): x^{2} + y^{2} < 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2acfd3c0-352a-50c7-b5bc-6d486c378ccf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121480} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c16386e-2f29-56bc-80ea-7a1f976538d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121477}] :question/id #uuid "2cb27705-2ef7-5315-a2e6-466639501b52" :question/math-academy-id "q-164232" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $x^{2} + y^{2} - z^{2} =-1$, find the domain of $z = z(x, y)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294587 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d28eda1a-a90b-57e9-969a-eb36552e413e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Traces of Hyperboloids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a38499c7-55c3-5a9e-8044-d0ea0a672683" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294589} {:answer/id #uuid "7ebbd4c0-da35-5e32-b98a-4f35891aef23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294590} {:answer/id #uuid "5b2f1fec-0431-54e9-8542-33a81f075805" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$9$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294591} {:answer/id #uuid "e377644e-ffd1-5050-9452-9d2ff27b4d62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$18$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294592} {:answer/id #uuid "ccde8264-6c46-5e45-a78b-6a583bab3808" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{6}$ and $\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a38499c7-55c3-5a9e-8044-d0ea0a672683" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294589} :answer-field/id #uuid "94346eb5-262f-588b-bef3-1a091bfda306" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294588}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5d31914a-9f1e-5783-b7aa-a38c819334db" :question/math-academy-id "q-164380" :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of two sheets $-\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{18}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+(z-2)^{2}=-1$ and the plane $z=3$ onto the $xy$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $z=3,$ we substitute $z=3$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{18}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+(3-2)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{18}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+1 & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{18}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{36}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{{6}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $6$ and $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124798 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d28eda1a-a90b-57e9-969a-eb36552e413e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Traces of Hyperboloids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9073e829-bdbc-5fd4-a768-fcfbbf3d1b09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$18$ and $50$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121811} {:answer/id #uuid "9dafa6ec-ac28-5d71-bf21-77c972391c2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$36$ and $100$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121812} {:answer/id #uuid "a52166f0-2ae6-5669-b785-5da2e7385da0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6\\sqrt{2}$ and $10\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121813} {:answer/id #uuid "205cbc13-72d2-5d5e-a8b5-659be22e32d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3\\sqrt{2}$ and $5\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121814} {:answer/id #uuid "7020ffe6-6830-52d3-b3b3-329346b550a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ and $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7020ffe6-6830-52d3-b3b3-329346b550a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ and $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121815} :answer-field/id #uuid "4447137c-128f-5cc4-a598-e9a08181bfea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121810}] :question/id #uuid "de878af4-60e8-5b69-ad9a-b8c3044d2e69" :question/math-academy-id "q-35410" :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{x^{2}}{8} + ((y - 4)^{2})/(18) - \\frac{z^{2}}{50} = 1$ and the plane $x = 2$ onto the $yz$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?"}]}
